## 4. Same-Month Comparison

```sql
WITH monthly AS (
    SELECT 
        strftime('%Y', date) AS year,
        strftime('%m', date) AS month,
        SUM(sessions) AS sessions,
        SUM(conversions) AS conversions
    FROM marketing_events
    GROUP BY year, month
),
calculated_rates AS (
    SELECT 
        year,
        month,
        ROUND(
            conversions * 100.0 / sessions,
            2
        ) AS conversion_rate
    FROM monthly
)
SELECT 
    year,
    month,
    conversion_rate,
    LAG(conversion_rate) OVER (
        PARTITION BY month 
        ORDER BY year
    ) AS previous_year_rate
FROM calculated_rates
ORDER BY month, year;
```

**Analysis:**  
This analysis compares our monthly conversion rates year-over-year (e.g., July 2025 vs. July 2024). By grouping the data by month and sorting by year, the query successfully tracks how performance for any given month has evolved compared to the same period in the previous year.

