## 5. Regional Performance

```sql
SELECT
    me.region,
    c.channel,
    SUM(me.sessions) AS sessions,
    SUM(me.conversions) AS conversions,
    ROUND(
        SUM(me.conversions) * 100.0 / SUM(me.sessions),
        2
    ) AS conversion_rate
FROM marketing_events me
JOIN campaigns c
    ON me.campaign_id = c.campaign_id
GROUP BY me.region, c.channel
ORDER BY me.region, conversion_rate DESC;
```

**Analysis:**  
I joined the `marketing_events` and `campaigns` tables to map traffic data to specific marketing channels. Then, I grouped the results by region and channel to calculate the total sessions, conversions, and conversion rate for each combination. Finally, I sorted the data by region and conversion rate from highest to lowest to make it easier to identify the top-performing channels in each region.
